1092
01:32:29,169 --> 01:32:31,087
I 'll tell you in the spring .

1093
01:32:31,129 --> 01:32:33,548
I 'm going to take you to the South of France .

1094
01:32:33,590 --> 01:32:37,719
To Antibes , St Tropez , anywhere you want to go .

1095
01:32:37,761 --> 01:32:40,472
And I 'm going to tell you the story of my life .

1096
01:33:07,749 --> 01:33:10,126
( DOOR CREAKS )

1097
01:33:15,006 --> 01:33:18,009
I never thought I 'd set foot in this house again .

1098
01:33:18,051 --> 01:33:20,762
If only we 'd been 3O instead of 20 .

1099
01:33:20,804 --> 01:33:22,472
What fools we were !

1100
01:33:23,598 --> 01:33:25,433
I don 't think anybody 's here .

1101
01:33:25,475 --> 01:33:27,310
She 's here .

1102
01:33:27,352 --> 01:33:28,812
I 'm sure of it .

1103
01:33:30,855 --> 01:33:32,607
You want to try upstairs ?

1104
01:33:37,445 --> 01:33:40,198
Nothing will come of this .

1105
01:33:40,240 --> 01:33:43,326
You want to stay downstairs , Mr James ?

1106
01:33:46,204 --> 01:33:47,831
Not on your life .

1107
01:33:49,082 --> 01:33:52,085
It 's hard to believe that all of this was so beautiful then .

1108
01:33:52,127 --> 01:33:55,338
The rooms downstairs and her room up here .

1109
01:33:55,380 --> 01:33:56,756
Just beautiful .

1110
01:33:56,798 --> 01:33:59,634
So was Alma 's .

1111
01:33:59,676 --> 01:34:01,219
Agh !

1112
01:34:03,847 --> 01:34:05,140
Ow !

1113
01:34:05,181 --> 01:34:08,810
( EERIE WHISTLE )

1114
01:34:13,439 --> 01:34:15,733
All right , that 's enough .

1115
01:34:17,068 --> 01:34:18,695
We 'll all go .

1116
01:34:18,736 --> 01:34:20,113
He can 't be moved .

1117
01:34:20,155 --> 01:34:21,948
Please , Sears , we 'll stay together .

1118
01:34:21,990 --> 01:34:23,575
Ricky , don 't argue with me .

1119
01:34:23,616 --> 01:34:27,162
I 'm too old , too tired and too frightened .

1120
01:34:28,454 --> 01:34:29,706
Sears !

1121
01:34:29,747 --> 01:34:32,500
I 'll be back with help as soon as I can .

1122
01:34:37,046 --> 01:34:39,966
I could never make him do anything he didn 't want to do .

1123
01:34:57,775 --> 01:34:59,152
You OK ?

1124
01:34:59,194 --> 01:35:00,778
Yeah .

1125
01:35:12,207 --> 01:35:14,500
All clear so far .

1126
01:35:17,921 --> 01:35:19,422
Can you hear me ?

1127
01:35:19,464 --> 01:35:20,715
Yeah .

1128
01:35:46,532 --> 01:35:49,285
( WOMAN GIGGLING )

1129
01:35:50,703 --> 01:35:52,121
Ricky ?

1130
01:35:54,874 --> 01:35:57,001
Ricky ?

1131
01:36:05,301 --> 01:36:06,761
Find anything ?

1132
01:36:08,638 --> 01:36:10,473
Just an empty room .

1133
01:36:11,683 --> 01:36:13,685
You OK ?

1134
01:36:13,726 --> 01:36:16,271
Yeah . I was just thinking ...

1135
01:36:16,312 --> 01:36:18,273
What ? About the sidewalks again ?

1136
01:36:18,314 --> 01:36:20,608
No , you scamp .

1137
01:36:20,650 --> 01:36:24,904
It 's Sears . I 'm worried about him .

1138
01:36:24,946 --> 01:36:28,658
A lot of people think I take too much guff from him .

1139
01:36:28,700 --> 01:36:29,951
But I don 't mind that .

1140
01:36:29,993 --> 01:36:33,413
It 's sort of permanent junior partnership stuff , you know .

1141
01:36:34,580 --> 01:36:35,957
What can I do ?

1142
01:36:35,999 --> 01:36:37,333
I 've been married to the guy

1143
01:36:37,375 --> 01:36:39,919
sure as I 've been married to Stella all these years .

1144
01:36:41,921 --> 01:36:43,464
He 'll be OK .

1145
01:36:44,799 --> 01:36:46,426
I wonder .

1146
01:37:15,580 --> 01:37:17,373
Agh !

1147
01:37:39,187 --> 01:37:42,065
( HE MOANS )

1148
01:37:51,908 --> 01:37:55,161
EVA : Dance with me , you little toad .

1149
01:37:55,203 --> 01:37:56,954
( HE SCREAMS )

1150
01:37:56,996 --> 01:38:00,083
( HOOTING )

1151
01:38:06,005 --> 01:38:08,132
( WIND WHISTLES )

1152
01:38:13,388 --> 01:38:15,515
Maybe he just got stuck in the snow .

1153
01:38:15,556 --> 01:38:18,017
He 'd have come back if he was all right .

1154
01:38:20,061 --> 01:38:22,271
I don 't like it .

1155
01:38:28,319 --> 01:38:29,821
We 'll end it , Ricky .

1156
01:38:29,862 --> 01:38:31,948
We 'll lay her to rest .

1157
01:38:31,989 --> 01:38:34,409
An old man and a pup , huh ?

1158
01:38:34,450 --> 01:38:36,035
We are the Chowder Society now .

1159
01:38:37,537 --> 01:38:38,913
( HE GROANS )

1160
01:38:41,791 --> 01:38:43,584
Sears was right .

1161
01:38:43,626 --> 01:38:46,212
You sound like Knute Rockne .

1162
01:38:48,965 --> 01:38:51,050
Have to get you to a doctor .

1163
01:38:56,222 --> 01:38:57,682
Be right back .

1164
01:39:33,050 --> 01:39:35,261
Thank goodness you came along .

1165
01:39:35,303 --> 01:39:37,305
Lucky for both of us , Ricky .

1166
01:39:47,231 --> 01:39:50,485
Don 't struggle or I 'll kill you right now , you hear me ?

1167
01:39:52,028 --> 01:39:54,739
- You 'll be quiet ? - Yeah .

1168
01:39:54,780 --> 01:39:56,949
There 's a good little rabbit .

1169
01:39:56,991 --> 01:39:58,868
Why are you doing this ?

1170
01:40:00,536 --> 01:40:03,456
Would you like to live for ever , Ricky ?

1171
01:40:04,665 --> 01:40:06,792
That 's what she promised us .

1172
01:40:06,834 --> 01:40:10,922
Imagine the peace of lying down with your hands across your chest .

1173
01:40:10,963 --> 01:40:12,465
You go to hell .

1174
01:40:15,343 --> 01:40:18,304
Imagine her waiting for you all these years .

1175
01:40:18,346 --> 01:40:21,933
Imagine her sleeping under ice and snow .

1176
01:40:21,974 --> 01:40:24,310
Waiting .

1177
01:40:24,352 --> 01:40:25,561
The pond .

1178
01:40:25,603 --> 01:40:28,064
Would you like to be immortal ?

1179
01:40:28,105 --> 01:40:30,441
Even if you must die first ?

1180
01:40:30,483 --> 01:40:32,652
Good lord ! She 's in the pond .

1181
01:40:32,693 --> 01:40:34,612
Alive .

1182
01:40:35,780 --> 01:40:37,448
Still alive .

1183
01:40:38,616 --> 01:40:41,327
She tricked you . You won 't live for ever .

1184
01:40:42,620 --> 01:40:46,123
- Live longer than you . - Oh , no , you won 't !

1185
01:41:03,724 --> 01:41:06,269
( EERIE MUSIC )

1186
01:41:06,310 --> 01:41:07,895
( RAT SQUEAKS )

1187
01:41:35,715 --> 01:41:37,633
( EVA GIGGLING )

1188
01:41:53,149 --> 01:41:56,068
( WIND WHISTLING )

1189
01:42:05,620 --> 01:42:07,580
( MOANING ECHOES )

1190
01:42:09,415 --> 01:42:11,500
( RUSTLING )

1191
01:43:03,803 --> 01:43:06,222
( SIREN WAILS )

1192
01:43:07,556 --> 01:43:11,060
You 're out of your skull . You know that , Mr Hawthorne ?

1193
01:43:12,520 --> 01:43:13,896
We 've got to hurry .

1194
01:43:13,938 --> 01:43:16,357
We 've got to help the boy .

1195
01:43:37,545 --> 01:43:40,756
( ICE CRASHES )

1196
01:43:51,475 --> 01:43:53,853
Aren 't you even going to say hello ?

1197
01:43:58,107 --> 01:44:00,317
Oh , Don , you disappoint me .

1198
01:44:08,951 --> 01:44:11,746
I thought you 'd be dying to see me .

1199
01:44:12,997 --> 01:44:16,125
( WHISPERS ) Y ... y ... you 're not here .

1200
01:44:16,167 --> 01:44:18,711
You 're not here .

1201
01:44:18,753 --> 01:44:22,715
Talk sense , Don . You can see me , can 't you ?

1202
01:44:22,757 --> 01:44:24,467
You can hear me .

1203
01:44:28,262 --> 01:44:29,638
I 'm here .

1204
01:44:29,680 --> 01:44:32,141
Get away from me !

1205
01:44:38,773 --> 01:44:40,900
Faster .

1206
01:44:42,026 --> 01:44:43,360
Poor Don .

1207
01:44:44,612 --> 01:44:47,490
Haven 't you been longing for me ?

1208
01:44:50,117 --> 01:44:51,744
Waiting for me .

1209
01:44:56,749 --> 01:44:58,709
I 've come for you .

1210
01:44:58,751 --> 01:45:01,170
You 're dead .

1211
01:45:01,212 --> 01:45:03,130
And you will be too ,

1212
01:45:03,172 --> 01:45:05,966
dead and wet and cold .

1213
01:45:15,434 --> 01:45:18,020
Don 't you want to make love to me ?

1214
01:45:23,067 --> 01:45:26,570
Don 't you want to know what you 've touched ?

1215
01:45:26,612 --> 01:45:28,364
( HE SCREAMS )

1216
01:45:39,667 --> 01:45:43,128
I will take you places where you 've never been .

1217
01:45:51,095 --> 01:45:54,723
I will show you things that you have neverseen .

1218
01:45:54,765 --> 01:45:56,100
No !

1219
01:46:01,230 --> 01:46:04,984
And I will see the life run out of you .

1220
01:46:06,193 --> 01:46:09,196
( SCREAMING )

1221
01:47:43,040 --> 01:47:46,126
( CHURCH BELL RINGS )

